.page nl 1 number the lines of files

# SYNOPSIS
*nl* [*-b* _STYLE_] [*-w* _N_] [*-s* _SEP_] [*-v* _N_] [_FILE_...]

# DESCRIPTION
`nl` copies its input, putting a line number in front of each line. By default only lines that are not empty are numbered; empty lines are left blank so the numbers stay with the text.

# OPTIONS
@ *-b* _STYLE_
    `a` numbers every line; any other value (the default is `t`) numbers only the non-empty lines.
@ *-w* _N_
    Width of the number field. The default is 6.
@ *-s* _SEP_
    The string put between the number and the text. The default is a tab.
@ *-v* _N_
    The number of the first line. The default is 1.

The option `-n` is accepted and ignored.

# EXAMPLES
    nl /Hakurei/etc/motd
    nl -ba -s': ' script.sh
    ls | nl -w3

# SEE ALSO
cat(1), wc(1), head(1)
